classDiagram
    %% PawPal+ class diagram. Keep this file updated so it matches your final implementation.

    class Owner {
        +str name
        +int available_time
        +dict preferences
        +list~Pet~ pets
        +add_pet(pet) None
        +set_available_time(minutes) None
        +update_preferences(preferences) None
        +get_all_tasks() list~Task~
    }

    class Pet {
        +str name
        +str species
        +int age
        +list~Task~ tasks
        +add_task(task) None
        +complete_task(task) Task
        +view_tasks() list~Task~
        +get_info() str
    }

    class Task {
        +str title
        +int duration_minutes
        +str priority
        +str frequency
        +bool completed
        +str pet_name
        +str start_time
        +date due_date
        +update_task(title, duration_minutes, priority, frequency, start_time) None
        +mark_complete() None
        +next_occurrence() Task
        +get_details() str
    }

    class Scheduler {
        +Owner owner
        +list~Task~ daily_plan
        +list~Task~ skipped
        +sort_by_priority() list~Task~
        +sort_by_time(tasks) list~Task~
        +filter_tasks(pet_name, completed) list~Task~
        +generate_schedule(for_date) list~Task~
        +detect_conflicts(tasks) list~tuple~
        +format_conflict(task_a, task_b) str
        +get_skip_reason(task) str
        +explain_schedule() str
    }

    Owner "1" --> "*" Pet : has
    Pet "1" --> "*" Task : has
    Scheduler "1" --> "1" Owner : plans for
    Scheduler "1" --> "*" Task : organizes into daily_plan / skipped

    note for Task "priority is low, medium, or high.\nScheduler maps it to 1, 2, 3 when sorting.\nfrequency is once, daily, or weekly.\nstart_time is 24-hour HH:MM, or empty for any time.\nnext_occurrence() returns None for once tasks;\ndaily/weekly copies are due 1 or 7 days later."

    note for Scheduler "detect_conflicts() only reports overlapping pairs.\nIt never removes or reschedules tasks."
